  D('avant-garde', {
    etymology:{origin:'avant-garde 经法语 avant-garde「先头部队、先锋」进入英语，由 avant「前面」与 garde「守卫、队伍」构成；军事隐喻后来用于艺术与思想创新。',prefix:null,root:{text:'avant + garde',gloss:'前方 + 守卫、队伍'},suffix:null,history:[],formationLogic:'比喻在文化、艺术或思想领域走在前面、尝试新方向的人群或作品。',mnemonic:null,note:'可作集合名词指先锋派或先锋艺术家，也可作形容词修饰其作品；通常带实验性。',source:'Etymonline — avant-garde'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'avant-garde.s1',domain:'现代艺术 · 运动流派',en:'The avant-garde collective staged a performance in which the audience chose the order of the scenes, challenging the idea that a play must follow a fixed script from beginning to end.',zh:'先锋艺术团体安排了一场由观众决定场景顺序的表演，挑战了戏剧必须从头到尾遵循固定剧本的观念。',structure:'The avant-garde collective / staged a performance / in which the audience chose the order of the scenes / challenging the idea / that a play must follow a fixed script from beginning to end.',grammar:'in which 引导定语从句；challenging 分词短语表示影响；that 引导修饰 idea 的同位语从句。',rationale:'观众决定顺序、打破固定剧本，是对传统艺术规范的实验性挑战，符合 avant-garde 的先锋义。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('The avant-garde movement rejected every experiment and required artists to copy one unchanging traditional form.','The traditionalist movement rejected every experiment and required artists to copy one unchanging form.','先锋艺术通常探索新形式；要求完全复制不变的传统形式与 avant-garde 的创新取向相反。')],
    quiz:[q('avant-garde',1,1,'A group of artists experiments with forms that challenge established practice. It may be called the?','avant-garde','autarchy','auditory','avant-garde 指在艺术或思想上走在前面、突破常规的群体。'),q('avant-garde',2,1,'An avant-garde performance is most likely to?','test an unconventional form or idea','repeat a traditional form without alteration','measure the height of a star','先锋作品常以实验形式挑战传统规范。'),q('avant-garde',3,1,'The original French image behind avant-garde is?','a group at the front of an army','a group listening to a lecture','a group waiting behind a gate','avant-garde 原指军队前方的先头部队，后比喻文化先锋。'),q('avant-garde',4,1,'Which use is correct?','The museum collected avant-garde works from the early twentieth century.','The museum avant-garded the works into a neat pile.','The avant-garde meant the works were easy to hear.','avant-garde 常作形容词修饰作品或名词指先锋派。')]}
  );

  D('avaricious', {
    etymology:{origin:'avaricious 由 avarice「贪婪」加形容词后缀 -ous 构成；avarice 来自拉丁语 avaritia，与 avarus「贪得无厌的」有关。',prefix:null,root:{text:'avarus / avaritia',gloss:'贪婪的 / 贪婪'},suffix:{text:'-ous',gloss:'具有……特征的'},history:[],formationLogic:null,mnemonic:null,note:'强烈贬义，常指对金钱、财富或权力永不满足的贪欲；语气强于 merely ambitious。',source:'Etymonline — avaricious; avarice'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'avaricious.s2',domain:'权力评论 · 财富扩张',en:'The avaricious governor sought not only larger taxes but also control of private mines, using public office to expand his personal wealth and political influence.',zh:'这位贪婪的州长不仅索取更多税款，还试图控制私人矿场，利用公职扩大个人财富和政治影响力。',structure:'The avaricious governor / sought not only larger taxes but also control of private mines / using public office / to expand his personal wealth and political influence.',grammar:'not only…but also… 并列贪求对象；using 分词短语说明手段；不定式表目的。',rationale:'不断追求财富和权力、利用职位满足私欲，体现 avaricious 的强烈贪欲义。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('The avaricious donor anonymously gave away every fortune and refused to keep any money or influence.','The generous donor anonymously gave away the fortune and refused to keep money or influence.','完全放弃财富且不求占有，不符合 avaricious 的贪婪特征；原句应使用 generous。')],
    quiz:[q('avaricious',1,1,'A business owner keeps demanding more wealth despite already having far more than needed. The owner is?','avaricious','austere','audible','avaricious 指对财富有过度、永不满足的贪欲。'),q('avaricious',2,2,'An avaricious official seeks both money and unchecked influence. The adjective conveys?','greedy desire for wealth or power','careful attention to other people’s needs','a sign of likely success','该词也可形容对权力的极端贪求。'),q('avaricious',3,1,'Choose the closest contrast.','avaricious and generous','avaricious and greedy','avaricious and covetous','generous 与贪婪相对；greedy/covetous 与 avaricious 近义。'),q('avaricious',4,1,'Which behavior most supports calling someone avaricious?','Taking extra money for oneself despite having enough.','Sharing a windfall with the whole community.','Declining an unfair bonus and returning it.','不知足地攫取更多财物符合 avaricious 的含义。')]}
  );

  D('averse', {
    etymology:{origin:'averse 经法语来自拉丁语 aversus「转身离开、避开」，是 avertere「使转离」的过去分词；其构词关联 ab-「离开」与 vertere「转」。',prefix:{text:'ab-（同化为 a-）',gloss:'离开、远离'},root:{text:'vertere',gloss:'转动、转向'},suffix:null,history:[],formationLogic:null,mnemonic:null,note:'表示不愿意、反感或不倾向做某事；常见结构 be averse to + 名词/动名词。',source:'Etymonline — averse'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'averse.s1',domain:'协商 · 风险偏好',en:'The lender was averse to extending the deadline without updated accounts, so the owners supplied a cash-flow forecast before requesting another month.',zh:'贷款方不愿在没有最新账目的情况下延长截止日期，因此业主在申请再延一个月之前提交了现金流预测。',structure:'The lender / was averse to extending the deadline without updated accounts / so the owners / supplied a cash-flow forecast / before requesting another month.',grammar:'be averse to + -ing；so 引导结果；before + -ing 表示先后。',rationale:'贷款方明确不愿在缺少账目的条件下延长时间，符合 averse 的不情愿义。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('The lender was averse to approving the loan and eagerly approved it before reading the application.','The lender was not averse to approving the loan and eagerly approved it before reading the application.','averse 表示不愿意、反对；“不愿意”与 eager approval 并置冲突，加入 not 才与后半句一致。')],
    quiz:[q('averse',1,1,'A patient is unwilling to take a medicine because of its side effects. The patient is?','averse to taking it','avid for taking it','attentive at taking it','be averse to 表示不愿做或反感某事。'),q('averse',2,1,'Choose the grammatically correct pattern.','She is averse to borrowing money.','She is averse for borrow money.','She is averse to borrow money.','介词 to 后接名词或动名词，因此用 borrowing。'),q('averse',3,1,'A manager averse to risk will usually?','avoid uncertain investments','seek the most uncertain investment available','approve every plan without review','averse to risk 描写不喜欢或回避风险。'),q('averse',4,1,'The Latin source of averse suggests?','turning away from something','hearing something clearly','assigning credit to an author','averse 的词源意象是转身避开。')]}
  );

  D('avid', {
    etymology:{origin:'avid 经法语 avide 来自拉丁语 avidus「渴望的、贪求的」，与 avere「强烈渴望」有关；英语常用于强烈兴趣或热情参与。',prefix:null,root:{text:'avere',gloss:'渴望、贪求'},suffix:null,history:[],formationLogic:null,mnemonic:null,note:'常见搭配 avid reader/fan/interest；可表示热情投入，不必然带贪婪或负面色彩。',source:'Etymonline — avid'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'avid.s2',domain:'户外生活 · 持续爱好',en:'An avid bird-watcher, Sora rises before dawn several times a week and records each species she sees without disturbing the nesting areas.',zh:'索拉是一位热衷观鸟的人，每周有几次天未亮就起床，并在不打扰筑巢区的前提下记录看到的每种鸟。',structure:'An avid bird-watcher / Sora / rises before dawn several times a week / and records each species she sees / without disturbing the nesting areas.',grammar:'avid + 活动爱好者；several times a week 表频率；without + -ing 表示避免的行为。',rationale:'定期投入时间观鸟并细致记录，体现 avid 的积极热情，而非仅仅暂时感兴趣。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('He was an avid reader who avoided books, disliked reading, and never opened one.','He was an indifferent reader who avoided books, disliked reading, and never opened one.','强烈热爱阅读与刻意避书、厌恶阅读相矛盾，应使用 indifferent 或 reluctant。')],
    quiz:[q('avid',1,1,'Someone who reads every evening and eagerly discusses books is an?','avid reader','averse reader','autocratic reader','avid reader 指对阅读有强烈兴趣并积极投入的人。'),q('avid',2,2,'An avid fan attends every home match and follows the team closely. The fan is?','very enthusiastic','unwilling to watch','a ruler without limits','avid 可描述长期、热情地参与某项活动的人。'),q('avid',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','an avid interest in astronomy','an avid to astronomy interest','avidly interest astronomy','常用结构是 an avid interest in something。'),q('avid',4,1,'In ordinary use, avid most often suggests?','strong enthusiasm or desire','a lack of sound','formal permission','avid 常表达强烈兴趣、渴望或热情。')]}
  );

  D('avocation', {
    etymology:{origin:'avocation 来自拉丁语 avocatio「转移注意、消遣」，与 avocare「把……引开」有关，由 ab-「离开」与 vocare「召唤」构成；现代义指主业之外的爱好或活动。',prefix:{text:'ab-（同化为 a-）',gloss:'离开'},root:{text:'vocare',gloss:'召唤'},suffix:{text:'-ation',gloss:'表示行为或结果的名词后缀'},history:[],formationLogic:'从把人从主业中暂时引开的活动，引申为业余爱好或副业。',mnemonic:null,note:'区别 vocation（职业、天职）；avocation 是工作之外定期进行的兴趣活动。',source:'Etymonline — avocation'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'avocation.s1',domain:'个人兴趣 · 主业之外',en:'Although she works as an accountant, restoring antique radios is her avocation; she repairs them on weekends and donates the finished sets to a local history museum.',zh:'尽管她的职业是会计，修复老式收音机却是她工作之外的爱好；她周末修理收音机，并把修好的机器捐给当地历史博物馆。',structure:'Although she works as an accountant / restoring antique radios / is her avocation / she repairs them on weekends / and donates the finished sets to a local history museum.',grammar:'Although 引导让步从句；动名词短语作主语；on weekends 表时间频率；and 连接谓语。',rationale:'会计是主业，收音机修复是业余定期从事的活动，符合 avocation。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('Her full-time occupation was teaching, and she called teaching her avocation because it was her only paid profession.','Her full-time occupation was teaching, while restoring furniture was her avocation.','作为唯一带薪主业的教学更应称 occupation/vocation；avocation 指主业之外的活动。')],
    quiz:[q('avocation',1,1,'A lawyer spends evenings restoring furniture purely for enjoyment. The restoration is an?','avocation','authorization','autopsy','avocation 是主业之外定期进行的兴趣活动。'),q('avocation',2,1,'Which activity is most likely a person’s avocation?','A hobby pursued beside a full-time occupation.','The person’s only paid occupation.','A formal permission to enter an office.','avocation 与主业相区别，通常是业余爱好或副业。'),q('avocation',3,1,'Choose the natural contrast.','Her vocation is nursing; her avocation is pottery.','Her avocation is nursing; her vocation is pottery, though she is paid for pottery only.','Her avocation is the permission to work.','vocation 可指职业，avocation 指职业之外的活动。'),q('avocation',4,1,'A historian calls amateur astronomy an avocation because it is?','a regular activity pursued for pleasure beside the main work','a government policy to cut spending','a guaranteed full-time salary','业余天文观测作为主业外兴趣，符合 avocation 的定义。')]}
  );

  D('avocational', {
    etymology:{origin:'avocational 由 avocation 加形容词后缀 -al 构成；avocation 来自拉丁语 avocatio「消遣、转移注意」，现代指主业之外的爱好或活动。',prefix:{text:'ab-（同化为 a-）',gloss:'离开（avocation 的词源成分）'},root:{text:'vocare',gloss:'召唤（词源成分）'},suffix:{text:'-al',gloss:'与……有关的形容词后缀'},history:[],formationLogic:null,mnemonic:null,note:'表示与业余爱好、副业活动有关；常与 vocational（职业培训或职业的）形成对照。',source:'Etymonline — avocation; OED — avocational'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'avocational.s1',domain:'社区教育 · 业余课程',en:'The library’s avocational photography course meets on Saturday mornings, allowing nurses, cooks, and office workers to practice composition without preparing for a photography career.',zh:'图书馆的业余摄影课程在周六上午上课，让护士、厨师和办公室职员练习构图，而不是为摄影职业做准备。',structure:'The library’s avocational photography course / meets on Saturday mornings / allowing nurses, cooks, and office workers / to practice composition / without preparing for a photography career.',grammar:'avocational 修饰 course；allow someone to do；without + -ing 表示并非职业准备。',rationale:'课程服务于主业之外的兴趣，并明确不以职业资格或就业为目标，符合 avocational。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('The vocational course taught licensed electricians the exact skills required for their paid jobs, so it was purely avocational.','The vocational course taught licensed electricians skills for their paid jobs, so it was vocational rather than avocational.','为带薪职业提供专门技能属于 vocational；avocational 指主业之外的爱好活动。')],
    quiz:[q('avocational',1,1,'A weekend painting class is designed for enjoyment, not professional training. It is?','avocational','autonomic','attributive','纯兴趣性质、非职业训练的课程是 avocational。'),q('avocational',2,1,'An avocational activity is usually pursued?','beside one’s main occupation, for interest or pleasure','as the only paid occupation','only under government austerity','avocational 与业余兴趣或主业外活动有关。'),q('avocational',3,1,'Choose the best contrast.','vocational nursing training and avocational pottery lessons','autocratic leadership and audible signals','attribution of authorship and aural memory','vocational 与职业相关；avocational 与职业之外的兴趣相关。'),q('avocational',4,1,'The suffix -al in avocational turns avocation into?','an adjective','a plural noun','a past-tense verb','-al 构成形容词，表示“与……有关的”。')]}
  );

  D('avoidable', {
    etymology:{origin:'avoidable 由 avoid 加形容词后缀 -able 构成，表示在采取适当行动时能够避开或预防的；avoid 的更早来源存在词典解释差异，此处不强行拆分。',prefix:null,root:null,suffix:{text:'-able',gloss:'能够……的、可以被……的'},history:[],formationLogic:null,mnemonic:null,note:'表示某种损失、错误或危险本可通过谨慎措施防止；不意味着所有不良结果都能完全避免。',source:'Etymonline — avoid; OED — avoidable'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'avoidable.s1',domain:'实验室安全 · 预防措施',en:'The spill was avoidable: the technician had been trained to secure the loose hose, but began pumping before checking its connection.',zh:'这次泄漏本可以避免：技术员受过固定松动软管的培训，却在检查接头之前就开始抽液。',structure:'The spill / was avoidable / the technician had been trained to secure the loose hose / but began pumping / before checking its connection.',grammar:'be avoidable 表示本可防止；冒号后说明原因；before + -ing 表示先后。',rationale:'已有培训且可先检查接头，说明通过合理谨慎步骤能防止泄漏。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('The broken glass was avoidable, even though it happened before anyone could possibly see or prevent it.','The broken glass was unavoidable if it happened before anyone could see or prevent it.','若事发前无人有可能发现或采取预防措施，就不能称为 avoidable；应依据可预防性判断。')],
    quiz:[q('avoidable',1,1,'A spill could have been prevented by tightening a loose hose first. The spill was?','avoidable','avid','attributive','采取可行预防措施即可阻止的事件是 avoidable。'),q('avoidable',2,1,'Which loss is most plausibly avoidable?','A loss caused by skipping a required equipment check.','A loss caused by an unforeseeable event no one could detect.','A loss that has already occurred centuries ago.','漏做必要检查而造成的损失本可通过检查避免。'),q('avoidable',3,1,'Choose the correct suffix meaning.','-able means capable of being done or prevented.','-able means a person who does something.','-able means a past event only.','-able 表示能够……的，因此 avoidable 是能够避免的。'),q('avoidable',4,1,'A report calls a delay avoidable when?','A practical step could have prevented it.','No one could have predicted or changed it.','It was deliberately scheduled.','avoidable 的判断依据是是否存在可行的预防办法。')]}
  );

  D('avoidance', {
    etymology:{origin:'avoidance 由 avoid 加名词后缀 -ance 构成，表示避开、回避的行为或状态；avoid 的更早来源并无一致、确定的词源拆分。',prefix:null,root:null,suffix:{text:'-ance',gloss:'构成行为、状态或结果名词的后缀'},history:[],formationLogic:null,mnemonic:null,note:'可指回避责任、讨论或不愉快情境，也可用于法律或税务语境表示利用规则安排来减少义务；需与违法的 evasion 区分。',source:'Etymonline — avoid; OED — avoidance'},
    contexts:[{senseId:'avoidance.s1',domain:'团队沟通 · 冲突回避',en:'Their avoidance of the budget question delayed the meeting: whenever a colleague asked about costs, the project leads changed the subject to the design schedule.',zh:'他们回避预算问题，拖延了会议进程：每当同事询问成本，项目负责人就把话题转到设计进度上。',structure:'Their avoidance of the budget question / delayed the meeting / whenever a colleague asked about costs / the project leads / changed the subject / to the design schedule.',grammar:'avoidance of + 事项；whenever 引导反复发生的情境；change the subject to 是常用表达。',rationale:'持续不讨论令人不适或棘手的预算问题，具体展示 avoidance 的回避行为义。',sourceType:'authored'}],
    mistakes:[m('Her avoidance of the difficult topic meant she raised it directly at every meeting and asked for a decision.','Her avoidance of the difficult topic meant she changed the subject whenever it came up.','avoidance 表示回避；主动反复提出问题并要求决定与回避行为相反。')],
    quiz:[q('avoidance',1,1,'A team repeatedly changes the subject whenever costs are discussed. This is?','avoidance of the budget issue','attribution of the budget issue','authentication of the budget issue','不断转移话题是不讨论预算，即 avoidance。'),q('avoidance',2,1,'A tax arrangement uses legal rules to reduce the amount owed. In some contexts this is called tax?','avoidance','evasion, necessarily','audition','tax avoidance 可指利用法律安排减少税负，具体含义与合法性须看语境。'),q('avoidance',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','avoidance of responsibility','avoidance to responsibility','avoidance from responsibility','常见结构是 avoidance of + 被回避的事项。'),q('avoidance',4,1,'In “avoidance of eye contact,” avoidance means?','the act of not looking directly at someone','a formal approval to look','the ability to hear someone','avoidance 描述有意或持续避开某行为或情境。')]}
  );

